# NDR - Name drive and user locations

```text
RSX LOAD NDR
NDR name DU:
```

## Assign a name

```text
NDR ROOT A0:
NDR WORK D3:
WORK:
DIR ROOT:*.COM
```

Type NDR alone to list the names. Each names one drive/user, and several
names can refer to the same location. Delete an existing name with NDR
/DEL name before reassigning it. [PATH](PATH.HLP) resolves a name when
you add the entry.

## Save names

```text
NDR /SAVE D0:WORKSET
NDR /LOAD D0:WORKSET
```

/SAVE creates a new .NDR file. /LOAD replaces the live table with the
saved set. Use this pair to keep alternate configurations.

## Startup defaults

```text
NDR /DEFAULT A0:NDR.RSX
```

This embeds the current names in that writable provider file. The next
fresh load starts with those names. Use /CLEAR to empty the live table.
A warm boot retains live names while the provider is installed.
